        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/e9a140/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2022-01-27T09:34:49.017Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I’ll be running issue 2 of the Starter Kit (Void if Broken) next week or the week after, and I have a question about the “final boss,” the Voidheart.  Specifically, how the special actions work.  Instead of taking a basic action, the text says the Voidheart can summon a new dark hero AND advance the scene tracker.  Since it can also take two actions every turn, I would take that to mean that it could summon two dark heroes and advance the scene twice with every turn it takes, which seems very powerful.  In the Tactics section, it mentions that Overcomes can disable one of the VoidHeart’s special actions, but by my reading it only has one special action, it’s just that the one special action does two things.  So should the AND be an OR?  Or do they mean the special ability and the fact that it gets an extra action?  How have others handled it when they ran this issue?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-01-27T09:34:49.017Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 31,
        "readers_count": 30,
        "score": 21.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 29056,
        "topic_slug": "question-about-starter-kit-minor-spoilers",
        "display_username": "Gothire",
        "primary_group_name": null,
