      {
        "id": 242325,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-01-27T17:34:37.364Z",
        "cooked": "<p>By my reading, the Voidheart has two special abilities. One of these allows it to summon a minion and advance the scene tracker instead of taking a basic action, and the other allows it to take two basic actions per turn. I think each of those needs to be Overcome separately. It’s possible that the intent is instead that you can disable its summoning or its scene tracker advancing, but need to disable each separately.</p>\n<p>Secondly, yes, it looks like the Voidheart does have the power to summon two minions and advance the scene tracker twice as one action. However, it’s not required to, and a GM who felt that this will move things too quickly should probably only use the summon/advance once, and then either Attack the heroes or Boost the newly-summoned minion.</p>\n<p>If the players reached the Voidheart almost immediately, having it double-pulse on its first time is probably a reasonable tactical decision; this scene is a longer tracker with 11 spaces, presumably so that the players have time to shut the heart down. There’s also a good chance that they’ll be able to disable it pretty quickly, so it shouldn’t be a problem for long.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
